{
  "description": "Language-agnostic vectors of the `loft` shape, hand-computed on the sample figure at 1:100. The thigh bone `thigh-l` starts at the pelvis origin and hangs down in the pose `stand` (u = world -y, v = world +x ahead, w = world +z left); in `stride-left-forward` it is turned by 22 degrees about w (world angle -68 degrees, cos 68 = 0.3746065934, sin 68 = 0.9271838546), so u = (0.374607, -0.927184, 0) and v = (0.927184, 0.374607, 0). A section is the superellipse |x/rx|^n + |y/ry|^n = 1 in its own plane, drawn as `segments` points, point j at the angle 2 pi j / segments from the section's x axis: (rx sgn(cos) |cos|^(2/n), ry sgn(sin) |sin|^(2/n)). `limb` states the limb rotation [0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5] on every section (x = v, rx the half depth; y = w, ry the half width): a section at (a, b, c) reaches b - rx .. b + rx along v and c - ry .. c + ry along w. `plain` states no rotation and runs exactly along u, so x is w (rx the half width) and y is v (ry the half depth), exponent 4. Every extent is relative to the pelvis origin: elevation [ahead, up], front [left, up], plan [ahead, left]. stand, limb: ahead -0.05 (section 0) .. 0.02 + 0.04 = 0.06 (section 1), up -0.45 .. 0, left -0.08 .. 0.08 (section 0). stride, limb: ahead -0.05 sin 68 = -0.046359 .. 0.45 cos 68 + 0.02 sin 68 = 0.187117, up -0.45 sin 68 - 0.02 cos 68 = -0.424725 .. 0.05 cos 68 = 0.018730. stride, plain: ahead -0.05 sin 68 = -0.046359 .. 0.45 cos 68 + 0.03 sin 68 = 0.196389, up -0.45 sin 68 - 0.03 cos 68 = -0.428471 .. 0.018730. The depth that ranks the shape is its nearest point: the foremost in the front (0.06 for `limb` in `stand`), the highest in the plan (0).",
